  "facts": [
    "Ganter Bridge, finished in 1980, stretches 678 m across the Ganter River valley, making it Switzerland's second-longest spanning bridge after Poya Bridge.",
    "Its unique extradosed design features triangular concrete walls that enclose prestressed cable‑stays, protecting them from corrosion and giving the bridge a striking geometric silhouette.",
    "Between 2006 and 2008, the bridge underwent a full rehabilitation after south‑side piers shifted 105 mm, showcasing the engineering vigilance required at 1,450 m altitude."
